# Build context hygiene for repo-root-context image builds
# (deploy/compose/docker/*.Dockerfile).
#
# The host image copies platform/ and control-plane/ (brain profiles); the
# worker image also copies agents/ (agent SDK workspace); the dashboard
# image copies dashboard/. Those trees stay IN the context — only their
# junk is excluded.
.git
.agents
.claude
.opencode
audit-data
# tests/ is excluded wholesale for every repo-root-context Dockerfile
# EXCEPT tests/tools/Comuki.TestFakePi/ (add-agentic-test-contour WS6's
# worker-test.Dockerfile COPYs it to build the TestFakePi-based test
# worker image). A bare "tests" exclusion is terminal for buildah/Docker's
# ignore matcher — it never descends into an excluded directory to honor a
# later negation — so un-excluding one subtree needs the walk-down form
# below instead of a single "!tests/tools/Comuki.TestFakePi/**" line.
tests/*
!tests/tools
tests/tools/*
!tests/tools/Comuki.TestFakePi
openspec
**/bin
**/obj
**/*.user
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
dashboard/storybook-static
artifacts
